Two features disagreed about who decides `is_resolved`. confidence:F1 (ADR-0039)
derives Edge.confidence from (evidence_type, is_resolved) inside Edge.create --
at CONSTRUCTION time -- while ADR-0037 ruling 1 makes that producer value
ADVISORY, Edge.create defaults it to True, and ir.py's own field docstring says
"the producer-time value ... is ADVISORY; the finalize edge-resolution
sub-step's verdict is what serializes."

_finalize_edge_resolution duly flips the flag to False for every external dst
and left the stale number behind, so unresolved calls shipped at the RESOLVED
base: ast_call at 0.85 where the verdict says 0.40, ast_call_direct at 0.85
where it says 0.50. finalize.py's header even recorded "Edge.confidence
untouched" as deliberate -- a note written before confidence depended on the
flag at all.

MEASURED with production's own create_boundary_nodes + resolution sub-step:
caddy 6,167, mitmproxy 8,880, poetry 4,074, alertmanager 3,922 = 23,043 edges,
four repos, two languages, two evidence types. NOT a Go producer defect: any
producer that takes Edge.create's default and whose dst resolves external hits
it. The correction therefore lands at the one place that knows the verdict. The
filed remedy (pass is_resolved=False at the Go emit site) would have patched a
slice of a language-agnostic defect.

THE FILED MECHANISM IS A DIFFERENT, ALREADY-CLOSED DEFECT, AND BOTH OBVIOUS
MEASUREMENTS OF IT ARE TAUTOLOGIES. INV-fazim describes a live taint FP channel
-- an edge carrying is_resolved=True at an external dst reaching the ungated
bare-name fallback. Probing AFTER finalize finds 0 of 125,007 such edges across
9 repos, because finalize defines that predicate away. Probing BEFORE finalize
also finds none, because the flag has not flipped yet. Neither zero is evidence.
Closing the item on the post-finalize null would have repeated the INV-nufob
false-close exactly; two independent adversarial re-measurements inverted that
proposed closure.

DIRECTION: strictly downward and confined to unresolved edges. Measured on
caddy: 6,140 down, 0 UP, and 0 resolved edges changed at all.
receiver_blind_magnets bands at 0.80 and was the obvious exposure, but its
contract requires is_resolved to be TRUE, so this change cannot add or remove a
magnet finding -- structurally, not merely observationally. Its 0-in-both-arms
reading was an unexercised instrument and is reported as such rather than as
evidence of safety. slice's min_confidence defaults to 0.0, so no default view
loses an edge.

DELIBERATELY NOT TOUCHED, each with its own test: an explicit producer
confidence keeps its value (ADR-0039 -- re-deriving it would replace a
considered judgement with a table lookup); rank_score is re-mirrored only while
it still equals the old confidence, since ruling 3 says it diverges once a
producer relocates a ranking adjustment onto it. An evidence type with no
resolution split (ast_import, 0.95 either way) and one with no seed at all are
both no-ops. Idempotent, so the sub-step is safe to re-enter.

DOES NOT CLOSE INV-fazim. The item's own statement describes the taint FP
channel, which is closed by different means; this fixes the defect the
re-measurement found underneath it. The filing is refiled with this mechanism.

